  "includeThoughts": false,
  "publishChannels": [],
  "semanticKeywords": "•\tRegisters a query_intervals tool for high-volume sub-daily data, added as a second tool rather than a second Knowledge Base, since interval data is too granular to store as narratives.\n•\tAnswers demand-driver questions, for example “what drove the demand spike on the afternoon of August 3,” using granularity the Energy Agent does not have.\n•\tTies usage to equipment, for example “how much of last month's gas usage is attributable to the boiler,” when bills are paired with equipment lists and engineering ratios.\n•\tBenefits from weather-normalization data (NOAA / weather-station records) so trend answers adjust for cooling- and heating-degree-days rather than over- or understating usage.\n•\tStays on demand events that have already occurred and the systems that caused them; demand exposure that has not yet happened, and its financial consequence, routes to the Risk Agent.\n•\tInherits tenant isolation through the same five-layer enforcement: JWT claims, IAM, retrieval filter, row-level security, and S3 prefix scope.",
  "semanticUseCases": "The Facilities Agent is the operational lane: it explains why a building is behaving as it is by reaching past bill-level data into the sub-daily detail InSite already holds. It pairs Building Automation System and interval data with equipment and asset records to answer anomaly-detection and demand-driver questions that monthly bills cannot.",
  "agenticWorkflowId": "63d7922d-0946-46b2-ace1-987a848b1aa5",
  "enableForAutoInvoke": false,
  "semanticSearchEnabled": true,
  "isAvailableForMigration": false,
  "schemaVersion": "1.0"
